Patch 2068 (fix line): pipeline warm-up. Every guest-FP pipeline a run builds is noted in pipelines.bin (beside
shader_cache.bin); the next run builds all noted pipelines on worker threads right after the device is up, while the
game boots, and keeps them: the game's own request for the same pipeline then gets the ready one at once.
PSO_WARMUP=0 turns it off.

J-Stars builds its pipelines when a draw first needs them, on worker threads (patch 2057), and a draw whose pipeline
is not ready is skipped: on every start the fight intros showed characters missing and wrong colours for a few
seconds, and new effects on some maps slowed the game the first time (the maintainer, 11-11). HITCH log with a warm
shader cache: 110 pipeline builds in one intro frame (99 ms), bench/exp/2026-11-11_1603-intro-cache2. pso_cache.bin
(PSO_CACHE=1) is not used for J-Stars (its second start stayed on the loading screen), so nothing else carried
pipelines from one run to the next. This is the v0.15 installer patch 0004 for v0.19, keeping the warmed pipelines
instead of releasing them.

Tested (US disc, auto-pilot Training intro, three starts in a row): start 1 notes 159 pipelines and its intro shows the fighter half drawn (pipelines still building); starts 2 and 3 build 159/161 noted pipelines in 0.1 s on 8 threads at boot, HITCH shows 0 pipeline builds in the intro instead of 77-110 (50-99 ms) (bench/exp/2026-11-11_1608..1611-psow1..3, 2026-11-11_1603-intro-cache2).

